cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LLMatter2D, please cite it as below, together with the databases and papers behind the data you used."
title: "LLMatter2D: retrieval-augmented LLM for the analysis and discovery of two-dimensional materials"
abstract: >-
  LLMatter2D grounds pre-trained large language models in curated, citable data on
  two-dimensional materials (DFT electronic structure, Wannier tight-binding models,
  geometry and ARPES observables) through a hybrid retrieval layer, and proposes new
  2D materials by decorating the eleven Archimedean lattices, screening them with
  tight-binding physics and exporting structures for DFT validation.
type: software
authors:
